Historical CSS1 regression fixture
=================================

The HTML and GIF in this directory are unmodified copies retrieved on 2026-11-02:
https://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/Test/CSS1/current/test5526c.htm
https://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/Test/CSS1/current/sec5526c.gif

Their byte lengths and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in provenance.json. The HTML
identifies its last modification as 1 December 1998. These two original files
contain no individual copyright notice; no notice has been removed.

The W3C CSS1 suite credits W3C, the National Institute of Standards and Technology,
and Case Western Reserve University:
https://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/Test/CSS1/current/

W3C's test-suite cover page supplies the BSD licensing option, unless otherwise
stated: https://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/Test/Overview.en.html#licensing
This fixture is used under that BSD option for software development and regression
testing. It is not an authoritative W3C test suite, endorsement or claim of full
CSS1 conformance. The official licensing explanation is available at:
https://www.w3.org/copyright/test-suites-licenses/

The JSON expectations are independently calculated from the declarations and
checked against Chromium and Firefox. They are not outputs from the PHP engine.
The original reference GIF contains browser chrome and a historical caption; it
is an illustration, not a whole-image pixel-equality oracle.

